course: dictionary
lesson: 11592
title: The word aperture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aperture is an opening, hole or gap. «The bird flew through a small aperture in the wall.» The word "small" and the idea of flying through tell you the aperture is a little opening.
explain: In photography and science, the aperture is the hole in a camera or telescope that lets light in. «The photographer made the aperture wider because the room was dark.» Wider means more light gets in.
explain: The size of an aperture can change. Check the meaning by putting "opening" in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
fact: «Aperture» means an opening, hole or gap.
fact: In a camera or telescope, the aperture is the hole that lets light in.
fact: A wide aperture lets in more light, and a narrow aperture lets in less.
fact: Your pupil works like a camera aperture: it gets wider in the dark and smaller in bright light.
fact: In photography, a wide aperture can blur the background so the main subject stands out.
exercise: «The castle wall had a narrow aperture for arrows.» What is an aperture here? | *An opening or gap | A tall tower | A heavy stone | A kind of wooden door
exercise: «The photographer made the aperture wider because the room was dark.» Why did she do this? | Make the photo smaller | Stop light getting in | To make the camera heavier | *To let in more light
exercise: Which is a good meaning for aperture? | A bright colour | *An opening or hole | A dark room | A loud noise
test: «When the sun came out, the scientist made the aperture smaller.» What happened to the aperture? | Painted red | Removed completely | Made bigger | *Made smaller, so less light got in
test: Which phrase is about changing the size of a camera's opening? | Feed the cat | *Adjust the aperture | Tall green grass | Loud music in the hall
exam: «A wide aperture blurs the background, so the flower stands out.» What does a wide aperture do to the background? | Lets in less light | Stops the camera working | *Blurs the background | Changes the flower's colour
